{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread","id":992607,"title":"The Kindred of the East / Hengeiyokai thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-24T16:14:09-07:00","id":992607,"title":"The Kindred of the East / Hengeiyokai thread","content":"So, what are your thoughts about it? i see a lot of either &quot;Love&quot; or &quot;Hate&quot; for this, so go ahead. have your subject to discuss here. personally, i got the Hengeiyokai book about an hour ago and im wondering if theres splat books or extra books for it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T19:05:05-07:00","id":992684,"title":"","content":"They both need extensive reworking, and also to focus on their respective games over a shared cosmology. The material in Blood and Silk that frames the final fight of the Wan Xian before they became the Hungry Dead also needs to reference something other than the forces of Huang Di fighting those of Chiyou, because that seems too contemporary, even as a hazy event ascribed in ancient traditions. Hakken also need to be rethought, since Garou are super-old and Bushido is really young in comparison, like only about one millennium compared to the dozens of odd ones that the Garou have lived through. If you go back far enough, they should have a different name.<br /> <br /> As for expansions for Hengeyokai, W20 Changing Breeds does a lot to update the material, but not quite enough; the Beast Courts require more time and effort than a brief add-on to really work over. Also, W20 CB and a great deal of other sources, such as Blood and Silk, tend to completely and utterly disregard the presence of Garou in the courts that aren't Stargazers, Hakken or Boli Zousizhe, whereas Hengeyokai allotted the possibility of Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:20:57-07:00","id":992728,"title":"","content":"I agree, Asia contains half of population of humanity, a quarter of the land area, and a third of the global GDP, so its major supernatural groups should get more attention. I would add Demon Hunter X and Hsien to the list too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:07:19-07:00","id":992797,"title":"","content":"Hengeyokai is a concept that just needs some reworking, but KoTE is too profoundly broken (in cultural concepts and execution) and too mechanically flawed and I just throw it out. I made my own set of eastern vampires (new clans and some bloodlines) that live in a series of five kingdoms based loosely on psuedo-Buddhist philosophies (but in practice allowing Hindi, Maori, Pinoy, Malay, Sino-Tibetian, Goreo-Japanese, Vietnamese etc. traditions) and works way, way better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 10-25-2016, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T05:31:38-07:00","id":992896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElizabethSterling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=992797#post992797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hengeyokai is a concept that just needs some reworking, but KoTE is too profoundly broken (in cultural concepts and execution) and too mechanically flawed and I just throw it out. I made my own set of eastern vampires (new clans and some bloodlines) that live in a series of five kingdoms based loosely on psuedo-Buddhist philosophies (but in practice allowing Hindi, Maori, Pinoy, Malay, Sino-Tibetian, Goreo-Japanese, Vietnamese etc. traditions) and works way, way better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:37:37-07:00","id":992961,"title":"","content":"I mean, it may work for your group, but that does not mean that it would work for the majority of other groups. While the mechanics of the KJ are odd, I have adjusted them enough now to allow them to function in future games. <br /> <br /> For example, I will allow KJ to add their Dharma level to their Virtues when testing to resist soul change. I will also make the difficulty of the Dharma rolls equal to the 5 plus (current Demon Chi \u00f72, rounded up) for the higher soul and 5 plus (current Willpower points\u00f72, rounded up) for the lower soul, allowing for a less confusing Dharma progression. There will also be a few more changes inspired by my discussions with people of the forums. The overall changes are relatively minor though, and I think that KJ could be mechanically fixed with just a few pages of errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:49:07-07:00","id":992988,"title":"","content":"When I say that 2nd ed Sabbat was full of crap, it doesn't matter, because there's a Revised edition that fixed it.<br /> <br /> KotE didn't get a Revised edition...so it stays full of crap.<br /> <br /> BUT, KotE was better than any 2nd ed book I got to read. AND, the Devil Tiger book was one of the best book I got to read...ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:20:24-07:00","id":993024,"title":"","content":"I actually preferred Thrashing Dragon to Devil Tiger, but each to their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:37:27-07:00","id":993104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=993024#post993024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually preferred Thrashing Dragon to Devil Tiger, but each to their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preference is irrelevant when both books are good. Or, were you referring to the dharmas' respective philosophies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:44:42-07:00","id":993142,"title":"","content":"The book and the philosophy are both preferable to me. Don't get me wrong, I think that all of the Dharma books, along with many of the other KotE books, are superior products, I just thought that Thrashing Dragons was the best of a superior gameline (unlike Demon the Fallen, which I thought was poorly produced, as well as disliking the gameline).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T00:50:42-07:00","id":995544,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one that thinks x8 is too much for Disciplines? They don't have the Clan restriction, but then it would make more sense for them to be x7 like non-clan Kindred Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T02:56:20-07:00","id":995566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=995544#post995544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one that thinks x8 is too much for Disciplines? They don't have the Clan restriction, but then it would make more sense for them to be x7 like non-clan Kindred Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I think it's meant to be because they're more powerful, but I actually think Chi resource management is enough of a balancer. They certainly aren't as powerful as Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:35:37-07:00","id":995627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread#post992607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what are your thoughts about it? i see a lot of either &quot;Love&quot; or &quot;Hate&quot; for this, so go ahead. have your subject to discuss here. personally, i got the Hengeiyokai book about an hour ago and im wondering if theres splat books or extra books for it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a big fan of Kindred of the East/Hengeyokai. I've run a number of games in Japan/China/Southeast Asia. One of my favorite aspects to that part of the gameline is that that setting was designed around the idea of different splats working together, and it's actually very easy (and hardly unheard of) to have a group with a Changeling/Hsien. a vampire, a werewolf, a wereshark and a mage and not feel like your group is the most special gathering of snowflakes of all time. Good luck balancing all that of course, but it can be pretty fun.<br /> <br /> And Faradn, I agree. I think x7 is reasonable. Kuei-jin disciplines tend to be slightly stronger than Kindred disciplines, and I think that's why they settled on x8. But it does feel a bit too pricey, and in my games I reduced the cost to a straight x7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-30-2016, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:59:57-07:00","id":995658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=995544#post995544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one that thinks x8 is too much for Disciplines? They don't have the Clan restriction, but then it would make more sense for them to be x7 like non-clan Kindred Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, WW did the same thing with Numina/Qiao in Demon Hunter X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:51:04-07:00","id":995970,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> So new to the forums and have a question. Is there talks about making a Kindred of the East 20 by chance?<br /> <br /> Also, my favorite Dharma as follows:<br /> <br /> 1: Devil-Tiger<br /> 2: Thousand Whispers<br /> 3: Song of Shadow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12573,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12573-kueijin","user":"Kueijin","date":". 10-31-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12573-kueijin","name":"Kueijin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12573_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T05:50:44-07:00","id":996039,"title":"","content":"Not anytime soon, from what I have been hearing. Interesting preference order, do you like any of the heretical Dharmas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:54:47-07:00","id":996124,"title":"","content":"Faces of God are pretty nifty, so are the Scorpion Eaters.<br /> <br /> And figured the KoE 20 wouldn't be out any time soon, just wanted to know if there has been any talk on doing a 20th edition for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12573-kueijin","name":"Kueijin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12573_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:01:13-07:00","id":996150,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but I would be more intrigued if instead of KOTE they just had a source material books that covered the known clans but had them adapted to Asian culture. Maybe not have a Sabbat/Cam. Who knows. I will be honest, when I first tried to read KOTE I just couldn't get into it, especially how it felt it was being shoved down people's throats with some of the source material for revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:39:08-07:00","id":996301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChristopherZacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996150#post996150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but I would be more intrigued if instead of KOTE they just had a source material books that covered the known clans but had them adapted to Asian culture. Maybe not have a Sabbat/Cam. Who knows. I will be honest, when I first tried to read KOTE I just couldn't get into it, especially how it felt it was being shoved down people's throats with some of the source material for revised.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By Revised you Mean &quot;came out well before revised and is based on stuff that goes back all the ways to the first suppliments in the line&quot; right? Even the Older stuff on Gaki, Bushi and the Cats doesn't have them being Cainites even if they might have used more similar mechanics(but so too did earlier Mages)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:33:39-07:00","id":996576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996301#post996301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> By Revised you Mean &quot;came out well before revised and is based on stuff that goes back all the ways to the first suppliments in the line&quot; right? Even the Older stuff on Gaki, Bushi and the Cats doesn't have them being Cainites even if they might have used more similar mechanics(but so too did earlier Mages)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, by Revised I mean the whole aspect of the Anarch free states being taken over by KoTE, Katana fights, and the Week of Nightmares...I understand you are referencing the stuff listed in the older by night books.<br /> <br /> What I am saying though in in Revised they were def trying to promote and push the KoTE line, well IMO. Oh, I forgot to use &quot;&quot; with a really long string of words...my bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:28:37-07:00","id":996610,"title":"","content":"I would actually like KotE to evolve into its own gameline. It is arguably more important than Demon or Orpheus, as it had more books than either of them, and I think that it is more interesting than Hunter. The Kuei-jin are interesting supernatural creatures and, quite frankly, they have an important role in cWoD, as they kicked the Kindred out of most of Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:44:44-07:00","id":996627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996610#post996610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually like KotE to evolve into its own gameline. It is arguably more important than Demon or Orpheus, as it had more books than either of them, and I think that it is more interesting than Hunter. The Kuei-jin are interesting supernatural creatures and, quite frankly, they have an important role in cWoD, as they kicked the Kindred out of most of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what, I could actually support that. If it was treated as it's own game line fine. I just didn't like how they tried to mesh it and VtM together. I know some people loved it and I totally respect that, just wasn't my cup of tea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:36:10-07:00","id":996681,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I am not quite sure why they tried to put them in with VtM. It is not like they put Orpheus or Demon with WtO or Hunter with MtA. I think that they could have just mentioned that the reason why the Kindred do not dominate Asia are the Kuei-jin, a race of competing supernatural predators, often erroneously considered to be the Kindred of the East, who have warred with the Kindred since the Antediluvians left the Second City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:16:58-07:00","id":996705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996681#post996681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I am not quite sure why they tried to put them in with VtM. It is not like they put Orpheus or Demon with WtO or Hunter with MtA. I think that they could have just mentioned that the reason why the Kindred do not dominate Asia are the Kuei-jin, a race of competing supernatural predators, often erroneously considered to be the Kindred of the East, who have warred with the Kindred since the Antediluvians left the Second City.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if it would have been presented that way I would have maybe been more open to it, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T14:32:52-07:00","id":996814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996681#post996681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I am not quite sure why they tried to put them in with VtM. It is not like they put Orpheus or Demon with WtO or Hunter with MtA. I think that they could have just mentioned that the reason why the Kindred do not dominate Asia are the Kuei-jin, a race of competing supernatural predators, often erroneously considered to be the Kindred of the East, who have warred with the Kindred since the Antediluvians left the Second City.</div> </div> </div> </div>That comparison is flawed. By the time Orpheus and Demon came out (and Demon revolved an awful lot around the dead in some respects), Wraith was dead (har dee har har), and Hunter doesn't have nearly enough postmodernism in it to line up with Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-01-2016, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:16:29-07:00","id":996837,"title":"","content":"Yes, WtO was dead (which is sad, considering that the premise had such promise, the idea of hundreds of millions of supernatural creatures just on the other side of the shadows with interesting), but Orpheus and Demon were literally born from the events that ravaged the Underworld, the Sixth Maelstrom, so they could both been considered part of the WtO gameline. As for HTR and MtA, I think that the Hunters are experiencing an inferior Awakening, as their Avatars (the Messengers) are being mutilated by an external force (perhaps the Corruption of the Wyrm is causing the 'birth' of unread Avatars or something), so the Hunters could be considered to be stillborn Mages. Just a thought....<br /> <br /> I do think that Onyx Path should think consider launching KotE as its own gameline, perhaps naming it Kuei-jin: the Damnation (or something or the sort). The name is a combination of Han and Japanese words, so it would be used as a pan-Asian name (with each region having their own names). I am sure that they could find a few dozen people who would be willing to work on it in this forum if they asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:12:49-07:00","id":996914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996837#post996837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, WtO was dead (which is sad, considering that the premise had such promise, the idea of hundreds of millions of supernatural creatures just on the other side of the shadows with interesting), but Orpheus and Demon were literally born from the events that ravaged the Underworld, the Sixth Maelstrom, so they could both been considered part of the WtO gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they have to do with ghosts in day to day operation. Of course, by that logic, Hunter would be a sub-game of Wraith, too, since they spent most of their time dealing with walking dead quasi-risen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for HTR and MtA, I think that the Hunters are experiencing an inferior Awakening, as their Avatars (the Messengers) are being mutilated by an external force (perhaps the Corruption of the Wyrm is causing the 'birth' of unread Avatars or something), so the Hunters could be considered to be stillborn Mages. Just a thought.... </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-code=\"pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pEZgJyTzqPg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> In addition to Werewolf intensely disagreeing with Mage on the level of metaphysics, Hunter also does, as Mage posits that all humans have a latent avatar and can be awakened as mages, but Hunter says that only humans with no ties to monsters or other weird phenomena can become imbued. The Messengers just don't tap anyone else, and also, they're two beings of rather extreme power, and can probably punk most beings with stats. They're not &quot;lesser mages&quot; but intentionally lower-key anti-monsters, because the ancient heroes that they're (read, most of humanity) descended from got rather far out of control with power..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do think that Onyx Path should think consider launching KotE as its own gameline, perhaps naming it Kuei-jin: the Damnation (or something or the sort). The name is a combination of Han and Japanese words, so it would be used as a pan-Asian name (with each region having their own names). I am sure that they could find a few dozen people who would be willing to work on it in this forum if they asked. </div> </div> </div>No, the &quot;pan-Asian&quot; name (which is just Mandarin and Japanese, so you're leaving out an awful lot of Asia there) needs to go, no matter what, because there need to be examples of similar phenomena making Hungry Dead around the world, or else we're just repeating the same problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:52:09-07:00","id":996932,"title":"","content":"Kindred of the East was really good overall.<br /> Yeah, White Wolf botched on several cultural aspects and such... but honestly that was expected.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The one thing I couldn't stand was the P'o... and giving that potentially to another player to basically play.<br /> That was not a a good move and is quite frankly a bad idea for several reasons... all player related.<br /> The idea of the P'o as an active adversary on the other hand was a good one.<br /> I just kept a lid on potential issues between players by acting as the P'o for each player character while I DM'ed.<br /> <br /> The whole thing with the Dharmas and them being capable/expected to climb the ladder to greater understanding and power... THAT was awesome.<br /> Overall, they should have been treated a bit different than just as vampires of the east, but that's not to hard to change.<br /> In most instances I found that their disciplines are weaker to a degree, not as flexible or have inherent drawbacks compared to those of the Kindred.<br /> Their lack of a distinct discipline enhancing their raw strength is putting them on the wrong foot against vampires and most shapeshifter.<br /> There is also the issue that they have to mix and match their Yin and Yang intake and where they stand overall.<br /> Overall, the Kuei-jin could be quite awesome, but I had the best results for my game when I rolled the Kuei-jin and Mummies basically together into one package<br /> and found that a more or less perfect solution.<br /> Thematically they are a PERFECT fit and quite frankly turning the Kuei-jin into immortal spirits fallen from grace and now trying to claw their way back, makes so damn much sense.<br /> Even better the expanded options aren't going to turn them into overpowered beasts.<br /> <br /> While I loved the concept of the mummy game line I found their different factions, unlike the general positive theme, not that evocative and rather generic,<br /> the Kuei-jin on the other hand with their dharmas and strange moral codes didn't have that problem.<br /> <br /> Now let's talk about the big one that concerns BOTH Kindred of the East and Mummy:<br /> Both were rather centered on their areas and that's that, this led to a kinda messed up naming convention in case of Kindred of the East and several other fumbles in regards to location descriptions, cultural stuff and so on... also once again the whole skilltastic catastrophe that is brawl vs martial arts. If there ever was bullshit in the games it is that one.<br /> Originwise it would have been better if they would have opened up the whole world for Kindred of the East gamers, instead of limiting it to most parts of Asia and a speck here and there.<br /> For the Mummy game line they did try to do that with the Player's companion, with varying success but at least they gave it a shot.<br /> If they ever modernize those lines or go for the whole 20th anniversary treatment, they would have to rewrite a good chunk here and there to make it palatable.<br /> It could be done and it wouldn't be too much work, since a solid foundation is already in place, still it would need to be adressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:58:02-07:00","id":996959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996837#post996837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, WtO was dead (which is sad, considering that the premise had such promise, the idea of hundreds of millions of supernatural creatures just on the other side of the shadows with interesting), but Orpheus and Demon were literally born from the events that ravaged the Underworld, the Sixth Maelstrom, so they could both been considered part of the WtO gameline. As for HTR and MtA, I think that the Hunters are experiencing an inferior Awakening, as their Avatars (the Messengers) are being mutilated by an external force (perhaps the Corruption of the Wyrm is causing the 'birth' of unread Avatars or something), so the Hunters could be considered to be stillborn Mages. Just a thought....</div> </div> </div> </div>What?! No, you're wrong about that. All the Post-Reckoning or Revised Era game lines (HtR, DtF, MtR and Orpheus) were all tied to WtO and the Sixth Great Maelstrom that ended it. The 6GM cracked the Abyss, allowing the Fallen to escape. Anubis conned the Ferrymen into manipulating the Hierarchy into the events that triggered the 6GM so that Osiris would awaken, giving rise to the Mummies of MtR. Orpheus is the spiritual successor of WtO. As for HtR? Thousands of wraiths were cast out of the Underworld and trapped in the Skinlands by the Shroud hardening into the Stormwall, resulting in a massive flux of ghosts and Risen. As a result the last two angels on Earth, known commonly as the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Lady, realize just how truly bad things have gotten and take one gamble to save the world by sending out the Messengers to Imbue people with the power to battle the darkness of the world as they had thousands of years ago before that ended in disaster.<br /> <br /> Which caused them to become the first of the Kuei-jin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996932#post996932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East was really good overall.<br /> Yeah, White Wolf botched on several cultural aspects and such... but honestly that was expected.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The one thing I couldn't stand was the P'o... and giving that potentially to another player to basically play.<br /> That was not a a good move and is quite frankly a bad idea for several reasons... all player related.<br /> The idea of the P'o as an active adversary on the other hand was a good one.<br /> I just kept a lid on potential issues between players by acting as the P'o for each player character while I DM'ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? You're confusing the P'o of KotE with the Shadow of WtO (which is called P'o in the Dark Kingdom of Jade). They are similar but not quite the same. The only time the KotE rulebook talks about Shadowguiding in KotE is in a sidebar as a suggestion. At no point does it make Shadowguiding as an actual part of KotE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996932#post996932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole thing with the Dharmas and them being capable/expected to climb the ladder to greater understanding and power... THAT was awesome.<br /> Overall, they should have been treated a bit different than just as vampires of the east, but that's not to hard to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get that. The Kuei-jin are a different breed of vampires. It's in the name of the game, <i>Kindred</i> of the East. Why change what they are? If you make them not vampires than why bother making it Kindred of the East?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996932#post996932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most instances I found that their disciplines are weaker to a degree, not as flexible or have inherent drawbacks compared to those of the Kindred.<br /> Their lack of a distinct discipline enhancing their raw strength is putting them on the wrong foot against vampires and most shapeshifter.<br /> There is also the issue that they have to mix and match their Yin and Yang intake and where they stand overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there is a Discipline that increases Strength, the Demon Shintai which not only boosts Strength (and to a lesser degree Dexterity and Stamina) but add demonic characters to them that further boost their combat abilities. So Kuei-jin with Demon Shintai 3 would see the Kuei-jin get +3 Strength, +1 Dexterity and +1 Stamina along with three demonic features which can further strength their combat abilities.<br /> <br /> Kuei-jin vs Cainites actually tends to favor the Kuei-jin in typical battle between two of similar age. Plus the Kuei-jin have more common access to the Umbra and Underworld, adding other avenues for attack that most Cainites can't use.<br /> <br /> As for Kuei-jin vs Werewolves and Shapeshifters, yeah but then that's pretty common among most splats against the Shapeshifters. Werewolves are the combat tanks of the playable splats in WoD. Most of the other splats aren't going to be able to stand up to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:17:54-07:00","id":996995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996959#post996959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Kuei-jin vs Werewolves and Shapeshifters, yeah but then that's pretty common among most splats against the Shapeshifters. Werewolves are the combat tanks of the playable splats in WoD. Most of the other splats aren't going to be able to stand up to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the things that they have to fight. Nexus Crawlers and their equivalents among the other two sides of the Triat are probably capable of ending a fight with vampires in their favor in no more turns than there are vampires, and damaging them sufficiently would be a chore, since they could have 80 Essence or more... and they aren't even the ones with the highest pools there among statted out spirits. Dream Makers be crazy, yo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:28:12-07:00","id":997091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996932#post996932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East was really good overall.<br /> Yeah, White Wolf botched on several cultural aspects and such... but honestly that was expected.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The one thing I couldn't stand was the P'o... and giving that potentially to another player to basically play.<br /> That was not a a good move and is quite frankly a bad idea for several reasons... all player related.<br /> The idea of the P'o as an active adversary on the other hand was a good one.<br /> I just kept a lid on potential issues between players by acting as the P'o for each player character while I DM'ed.<br /> <br /> The whole thing with the Dharmas and them being capable/expected to climb the ladder to greater understanding and power... THAT was awesome.<br /> Overall, they should have been treated a bit different than just as vampires of the east, but that's not to hard to change.<br /> In most instances I found that their disciplines are weaker to a degree, not as flexible or have inherent drawbacks compared to those of the Kindred.<br /> Their lack of a distinct discipline enhancing their raw strength is putting them on the wrong foot against vampires and most shapeshifter.<br /> There is also the issue that they have to mix and match their Yin and Yang intake and where they stand overall.<br /> Overall, the Kuei-jin could be quite awesome, but I had the best results for my game when I rolled the Kuei-jin and Mummies basically together into one package<br /> and found that a more or less perfect solution.<br /> Thematically they are a PERFECT fit and quite frankly turning the Kuei-jin into immortal spirits fallen from grace and now trying to claw their way back, makes so damn much sense.<br /> Even better the expanded options aren't going to turn them into overpowered beasts.<br /> <br /> While I loved the concept of the mummy game line I found their different factions, unlike the general positive theme, not that evocative and rather generic,<br /> the Kuei-jin on the other hand with their dharmas and strange moral codes didn't have that problem.<br /> <br /> Now let's talk about the big one that concerns BOTH Kindred of the East and Mummy:<br /> Both were rather centered on their areas and that's that, this led to a kinda messed up naming convention in case of Kindred of the East and several other fumbles in regards to location descriptions, cultural stuff and so on... also once again the whole skilltastic catastrophe that is brawl vs martial arts. If there ever was bullshit in the games it is that one.<br /> Originwise it would have been better if they would have opened up the whole world for Kindred of the East gamers, instead of limiting it to most parts of Asia and a speck here and there.<br /> For the Mummy game line they did try to do that with the Player's companion, with varying success but at least they gave it a shot.<br /> If they ever modernize those lines or go for the whole 20th anniversary treatment, they would have to rewrite a good chunk here and there to make it palatable.<br /> It could be done and it wouldn't be too much work, since a solid foundation is already in place, still it would need to be adressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did you combine Mummy and KotE, out of curiosity? I've suggested it another thread and would be interested to see how others do it<br /> <br /> As for Mage versus Hunter cosmology: easily reconcileable. Hunters have existed at least twice before. The first lot became the Wan Kuei. The second lot were the Inquisitors of Dark Ages. The Messengers are, or are related to, the Psychopomps who used to match mages with their Avatars. The two Ministers who rule them are understood as angels but probably predate that paradigm. They may have been the beings sleeping beneath Enoch, and were thus reawakened by the 6GM<br /> <br /> My theory is that despite all the guff about the Imbued being human, they're just as supernatural as mages. The point is that just as werewolves' Avatars are connected to Gaia and changelings' are connected to the Dreaming, thus preventing those beings from Awakening (as they're Awake in their own unique ways), the Imbued's Avatars are bound up in their own duties, thus preventing them from becoming any other kind of Awakened being. <br /> <br /> If you look at Wraith, Mummy and KotE, every being does appear to have a multipartite soul. The Avatar is that god-shard or mystical element within the soul that reincarnates from life to life and which is activated or subverted (in the case of vampires) when that being is Awakened to some kind of supernatural existence. Hunters have one too, but it doesn't Awaken in the same way. Mages are Awakening to their potential divinity; other splats Awaken or have their Avatars enslaved to serve other purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T07:17:07-07:00","id":997122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=997091#post997091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mage versus Hunter cosmology: easily reconcileable. Hunters have existed at least twice before. The first lot became the Wan Kuei. The second lot were the Inquisitors of Dark Ages. The Messengers are, or are related to, the Psychopomps who used to match mages with their Avatars. The two Ministers who rule them are understood as angels but probably predate that paradigm. They may have been the beings sleeping beneath Enoch, and were thus reawakened by the 6GM<br /> <br /> My theory is that despite all the guff about the Imbued being human, they're just as supernatural as mages. The point is that just as werewolves' Avatars are connected to Gaia and changelings' are connected to the Dreaming, thus preventing those beings from Awakening (as they're Awake in their own unique ways), the Imbued's Avatars are bound up in their own duties, thus preventing them from becoming any other kind of Awakened being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Inquisitors, their nature and their powers are different from the Imbued. It's surprisingly common misconception that DA:I is just HtR in the Dark Ages but it's not.<br /> <br /> And honestly given the Imbued's backstory and nature, it actually fits them better if they don't have an altered Avatar. After all, all those vampires and werewolves and mages and whatever have made a big mess of the world so let the mortals, with a bit of help, be the ones to clean up the mess and set things right.<br /> <br /> Hell the Imbued, despite their powers and being touched by the supernatural, still count as Sleepers when it comes to witnessing Magic, something no other playable splat does.<br /> <br /> Also, just because you want a single, shared world for the WoD, doesn't mean you have to have every splat line up in same way, that all their natures are caused by X changing or being altered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T08:51:55-07:00","id":997170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=997122#post997122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the Inquisitors, their nature and their powers are different from the Imbued. It's surprisingly common misconception that DA:I is just HtR in the Dark Ages but it's not.<br /> <br /> And honestly given the Imbued's backstory and nature, it actually fits them better if they don't have an altered Avatar. After all, all those vampires and werewolves and mages and whatever have made a big mess of the world so let the mortals, with a bit of help, be the ones to clean up the mess and set things right.<br /> <br /> Hell the Imbued, despite their powers and being touched by the supernatural, still count as Sleepers when it comes to witnessing Magic, something no other playable splat does.<br /> <br /> Also, just because you want a single, shared world for the WoD, doesn't mean you have to have every splat line up in same way, that all their natures are caused by X changing or being altered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I was answering the question of how the gamelines could be brought together, which someone else raised. I was offering a solution rather than just going 'nope' and 'yield to the one true way'. You don't have to use the suggestion<br /> <br /> That said, I don't care whether the Imbued think they're supernatural or not. They have powers beyond those of everyday mortals, so they literally are *super* natural. They might be Sleepers, but that doesn't detract from their supernatural abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T10:54:50-07:00","id":997241,"title":"","content":"The Imbued are supernatural creatures. Whatever force created the Imbued, the creation of the Imbued probably takes a lot of supernatural power. It is probably easier to mutilate an Avatar into the proper shape than it would be to create the Imbued from scratch, which is why I think that the Imbued are actually created from the mutilated Avatars of mutilated Mages. In fact, I think that they were created to destroy the supernatural creatures of the cWoD in order to prepare the Earth for the invasion of the elder gods (or whatever you will) by destroying the supernatural creatures who would be unwilling to submit to the Elder Gods.<br /> <br /> While it has been mentioned before, imagine a scenario where an alien force, like the Elder Gods, is getting ready to invade the Earth. The first step in any invasion is to cause chaos and confusion within the ranks of any potential defenders. The events of the Sixth Great Maelstrom and the Week of Nightmares could be seen as designed to cause chaos and confusion among the supernatural community. The creation of the Imbued would represent a fifth column that would attack the supernatural community during its confusion, preparing the way for the Elder Gods, and the Imbued could be implanted with a kill code by the Elder Gods to prevent them from being turned against their creators. Just a thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:14:22-07:00","id":997301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=997241#post997241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Imbued are supernatural creatures. Whatever force created the Imbued, the creation of the Imbued probably takes a lot of supernatural power. It is probably easier to mutilate an Avatar into the proper shape than it would be to create the Imbued from scratch,</div> </div> </div> </div>The other thing being an option is something that Hunter never devotes any time to entertaining. They're made from mortals because mortals all have the blood of heroes running through them and just have to act when the moment comes to realize it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> which is why I think that the Imbued are actually created from the mutilated Avatars of mutilated Mages. In fact, I think that they were created to destroy the supernatural creatures of the cWoD in order to prepare the Earth for the invasion of the elder gods (or whatever you will) by destroying the supernatural creatures who would be unwilling to submit to the Elder Gods<br /> <br /> While it has been mentioned before, imagine a scenario where an alien force, like the Elder Gods, is getting ready to invade the Earth. The first step in any invasion is to cause chaos and confusion within the ranks of any potential defenders. The events of the Sixth Great Maelstrom and the Week of Nightmares could be seen as designed to cause chaos and confusion among the supernatural community. The creation of the Imbued would represent a fifth column that would attack the supernatural community during its confusion, preparing the way for the Elder Gods, and the Imbued could be implanted with a kill code by the Elder Gods to prevent them from being turned against their creators. Just a thought... </div> </div> </div>...or maybe all of that applies to mages instead. They are dangerous reality warpers, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T16:53:56-07:00","id":997437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996959#post996959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? You're confusing the P'o of KotE with the Shadow of WtO (which is called P'o in the Dark Kingdom of Jade). They are similar but not quite the same. The only time the KotE rulebook talks about Shadowguiding in KotE is in a sidebar as a suggestion. At no point does it make Shadowguiding as an actual part of KotE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yupp... sorry, I haven't read the books in a long time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996959#post996959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get that. The Kuei-jin are a different breed of vampires. It's in the name of the game, <i>Kindred</i> of the East. Why change what they are? If you make them not vampires than why bother making it Kindred of the East?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't suggest making them NOT vampires of some sort, but I would have loved it if they had gone the whole way and make them even more different.<br /> In some of the supplements they tried to do that, which made them more interesting.<br /> Furthermore, as fallen agents of a higher power it would have been even better thematically... but that's just my opinion.<br /> I am probably also not conveying what I try to say that good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=996959#post996959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually there is a Discipline that increases Strength, the Demon Shintai which not only boosts Strength (and to a lesser degree Dexterity and Stamina) but add demonic characters to them that further boost their combat abilities. So Kuei-jin with Demon Shintai 3 would see the Kuei-jin get +3 Strength, +1 Dexterity and +1 Stamina along with three demonic features which can further strength their combat abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Demon-Shintai is awesome, but compared to potence or fortitude it brings a potentially nasty risk of rousing the P'o with it.<br /> Thoroughly awesome as a discipline, especially for making vampires shitting bricks in full on panic mode, but unlike Potence or Fortitude it carries a risk for using it.<br /> It is also not as focused as Potence when it comes to higher level abilities... and it is certainly not subtle.<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=997091#post997091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did you combine Mummy and KotE, out of curiosity? I've suggested it another thread and would be interested to see how others do it</div> </div> </div> </div>It was rather easy, honestly.<br /> I just took the parts of Kindred of the East and Mummy that I didn't like... primarily the limited origin options, due to geographical limitations and put my own spin on it.<br /> The Kindred of the East had already the fluff piece going for them that they escaped hell or something along those lines... depending how one used that or which cosmology was overall in play.<br /> Mummies had the whole &quot;spirit seeks roomie to crash with&quot; shtick going for them.<br /> Throw in a dash of Demon... and voila.<br /> In short: Wherever you hailed from it doesn't really matter, but you could be approached by a spirit/demon/whateveryouwanttocallit and you get a one time offer.<br /> Offer some headspace, get free from a place of eternal torment or at least that whole boring as hell experience of being dead.<br /> You get a second shot at life, awesome powers, even scarier enemies and some part of your psyche got fucked up royally by the P'o.<br /> Or to be more precise a true demonic soul seeking to escape it's very own hell.<br /> The KotE/Mummy mashup is now immortal... or at least can get better if killed.<br /> They have to choose a Dharma, which can vary wildly depending where you return or who gets to mentor you.<br /> Balance is gone, instead Dharma is the measuring stick... as well, as needing the opposing forces of Yin or Yang to keep going.<br /> Also: rename Yin and Yang to something more approbiate according to region and time. A old germanic tribal warrior would probably just name those forces life and death and be done with it.<br /> All Hekau Paths are usually inherently tied to Yang, with the exception of Necromancy which uses Yin and Nomenclature which can use both without issue.<br /> <br /> Also, Demon Arts are frowned upon in certain cultural circles, but that's rather specific... and does not necessarily hold true for the more subtle ones.<br /> And also the older bastards are not necessarily adhering to their own rules... freakin' hypocrites.<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> They also have all the shortcomings and advantages of typical KotE, which means Yin and Yang imbalance are in play, as well as the different conditions they can experience.<br /> All disciplines and Hekau cost x7, because x8 is a bit to expensive. They have neither disciplines or Hekau that are easier to acquire, unlike KotE or Mummies.<br /> I'll also note that I retooled Demon: The Fallen, as hinted at a bit up there, just slightly to get things in synch, but that's another thing.<br /> <br /> Oh and the Akuma... those are the interesting ones.<br /> They are only called Akumas - at least in parts of Asia - due to the fact that NOBODY likes them and wants them gone.<br /> They exchanged their immortality for penance and immunity to the ravaging of the P'o, which means their monster can't rear it's head.<br /> They are hunting down the escaped souls and returning them to their rightful place.<br /> They are the Wardens and Headhunters send after all the escapees and some of the escapees even get turned to take up the gruesome task of dragging the guilty souls back,<br /> even if they kick, scream and try their level best to get away.<br /> Even better: They do loose their immortality, due to cutting a deal with some powerful entity, but said entity catches their soul every time they die and may send them back into the field.<br /> And in best White Wolf tradition it is hard to determine who is right and who is wrong overall.<br /> And the best part: Demons can now create them, although not control them, to use them as goons, allies or something else entirely.<br /> Although they do need the names of some willing demons to do so, which adds another complication.<br /> <br /> It produced a hell of a paranoid atmosphere in the games where I used these changes, because nobody knew for sure who worked for whom.<br /> And cutting through all the webs, lies, deceit and intrigues on top of all the political stuff going on is just awesome.<br /> Right now I am leading a campaign with this setup in roughly 900 AD in what will once be known as the HRE.<br /> It's utterly hilarious, because the players are surrounded by human nobles, some werewolves, a bunch of rat kin that want to kill everybody just because and some mortal &quot;wizards&quot; - actually psions straight ripped out of Aeon. It's a political mess and utterly hilarious if looked at from the outside, in game everyone is playing for keeps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","user":"Bhurano","date":". 11-02-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:46:15-07:00","id":997578,"title":"","content":"Actually the celerity/potence like discipline of the Kindred of the East is Black Wind, while the fortitude like Discipline is Iron Mountain. All Demon based Disciplines are connected to your P'o Rating, and using them could trigger a Shadow Soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12573-kueijin","name":"Kueijin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12573_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:29:59-07:00","id":998049,"title":"","content":"Yes, and KJ do not get to innately boost their Attributes (unlike Kindred), and they are required to purchase Shintai to gain access to that ability. Iron Mountain is a passive ability, so it does not trigger your Demon, as you do not spend Demon Chi to activate it usually (the exception being the sixth and ninth level powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:37:04-07:00","id":998053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=998049#post998049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and KJ do not get to innately boost their Attributes (unlike Kindred), and they are required to purchase Shintai to gain access to that ability. Iron Mountain is a passive ability, so it does not trigger your Demon, as you do not spend Demon Chi to activate it usually (the exception being the sixth and ninth level powers).</div> </div> </div> </div>They changed that in the Revised ST Handbook, unfortunately. Using Iron Mountain costs one per turn under those rules. Also, Beast Shintai is a Soul Discipline for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T22:00:10-07:00","id":998086,"title":"","content":"I will have to take your word for it, it is one of the few cWoD books I do not have. I do not see the use for the changes, so I think that I will keep to the original versions. It makes as much sense as requiring Kindred to spend one blood point per turn to maintain Fortitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T02:28:41-07:00","id":998152,"title":"","content":"Btw, the same book says something about black wind turns coming before celerity/yang prana turns...right? (I'm still confused about that part).<br /> <br /> It also made it possible to resist any mental disciplines (except obfuscate) with the P'o, and Yang KJ could treat bullets as bashing. That wasn't the case in the KotE companion.<br /> <br /> I guess the VtM ST handbook aimed at making KJ more lethal, while the KotE handbook aimed at making vampires mental disciplines more of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:44:04-07:00","id":998575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=998152#post998152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, the same book says something about black wind turns coming before celerity/yang prana turns...right? (I'm still confused about that part).</div> </div> </div> </div>It was probably some combination of Yang Prana 1 (which can increase your initiative order) and Black Wind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also made it possible to resist any mental disciplines (except obfuscate) with the P'o, and Yang KJ could treat bullets as bashing. That wasn't the case in the KotE companion.<br /> <br /> I guess the VtM ST handbook aimed at making KJ more lethal, while the KotE handbook aimed at making vampires mental disciplines more of a problem. </div> </div> </div>I see this great company, though without wars, is nonetheless filled with writers who don't communicate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:20:29-07:00","id":998852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=998575#post998575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was probably some combination of Yang Prana 1 (which can increase your initiative order) and Black Wind.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I believe it's worse than that. Yang Prana extra actions come next round, while Black Wind actions come the same round.<br /> <br /> So...the way I understand it, a KJ with black wind 2 can act 3 times successively without interruption (except against another BW user). Add to that Demon Shintai, mental resistance and any P'o focused KJ will catch any celerity vampire pants down.<br /> <br /> Kinda overwhelming...but the chi costs and the shadow roll makes it even...well, that's debatable...ghouls and shovelheads are way too overwhelming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=998575#post998575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this great company, though without wars, is nonetheless filled with writers who don't communicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably just that self-derision that is typical to vampire games when it comes to crossover rules. You're a vampire? well then, every other supernatural will wreck you.<br /> <br /> Now, what happens when &quot;two&quot; different vampires meet?...do it case-by-case:<br /> - You play Kindred? then KJ are fucking lethal.<br /> - You play KJ? then Kindred are fucking annoying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:59:03-07:00","id":998872,"title":"","content":"Black Wind was designed with a very specific paradigm in mind - it was supposed to be like Celerity, but a little bit stronger (you could choose to do more than get extra actions), but you wouldn't have as much Demon Chi, so you couldn't use it as often, plus activating it could send you into Shadow Soul which was not a good thing. So a little bit better, but more dangerous and you generally wouldn't want to (or be able to) use it as often.<br /> <br /> Then Celerity got nerfed, but there's not really an easy fix for Black Wind. If you nerf it the way Celerity was nerfed you'd basically break it. Very few Kuei-jin are going to have more than 3 or 4 Demon Chi (in contrast to pretty much any Kindred having 10 blood points) so spending 1 Demon Chi per Action doesn't work, plus Demon Chi is generally harder (and more dangerous) to regain, <i>and</i> you still have the whole issue with falling into Shadow Soul when you use it.<br /> <br /> Rather than being nerfed or changed, Black Wind needs to be redesigned from the ground up. The paradigm it was initially created around no longer exists. It's far too powerful in its current form when compared to similar effects, but there's no way to really nerf it without completely crippling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:46:27-07:00","id":998920,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that Black Wind should be a passive ability, granting either one extra Dexterity or one extra Strength (allocated before Initiative every turn), which would make it more flexible than Celerity or Potence. Each turn, you could spend one Demon Chi per turn to awaken the Black Wind. Awakening the Black Wind would allow a character to sacrifice their bonus die to increase their movement by a factor of (Black Wind+1) and would allow a KJ to defend against any attack that turn as a reflexive action, even if they are within fire soul. Each turn that the Black Wind is awakened, the KJ must resist shadow soul, though the Hun would gain one bonus die to resist shadow soul triggered by Black Wind per level of Black Wind. Demon Chi could still be spent independent of Black Wind to gain Strength successes or to take extra actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T09:15:44-08:00","id":999255,"title":"","content":"How about this: passive Black Wind works like Shadow dice for Dexterity or Strength dice pools. You can allocate the dice however you want each turn, but if this means you score more successes than your Hun rating at any time, you enter (or at least roll for) Shadow Soul. <br /> <br /> For the active power, spend one Demon Chi and gain your rating in free actions. Resist Shadow Soul as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-06-2016, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:35:38-08:00","id":999302,"title":"","content":"That would make Black Wind much more powerful than Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T23:55:34-08:00","id":999601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=999302#post999302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would make Black Wind much more powerful than Celerity.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's much riskier too. You're constantly at risk of Shadow Soul.<br /> <br /> Wraiths and the Risen get Shadow dice and it doesn't break that game, even despite the fact that Risen can also take Potence, Celerity and Fortitude. Arguably Shadow Soul is at least as dangerous to a KJ as Catharsis is to a Risen, but perhaps more so, since it can accompany a moment of blindness and send a vampire spiralling back into damnation. The Risen and his Shadow don't necessarily become mindless zombies if the Shadow gets some fun for a scene.<br /> <br /> I don't really think KJ should have to balance with Celerity. Garou and Rage don't, after all, and KJ are at their best when they have nothing to do with Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:28:22-08:00","id":999706,"title":"","content":"But the P'o is not the Shadow. The P'o is literally a demonic symbiote forged by the agony experienced by the animal part of the soul while the divine part of the soul was being punished. The Shadow is just the dark impulses of a Wraith given voice.<br /> <br /> Black Wind and Celerity were fairly well balanced in Revised, so I think that it should seek to maintain that balance. I have suggested one version that may keep the relative balance between the two Disciplines. I think that it is interesting to discuss it further though, and I hope that anyone working on KotE 20th will eventually look at our discussion.<br /> <br /> Now, I do think that it would be interesting to allow the Hun to be able to wrest additional Demon Chi from the P'o. Perhaps a PC could spend one point of Willpower to make a contested roll between the P'o and Hun (difficulty 6). If the Hun succeeds, each net success gives the KJ one point of Demon Chi. If the P'o succeeds, the KJ enters Shadow Soul for a scene. If neither succeeds, the KJ is paralyzed for one turn. If the Hun botches, the KJ must make a negative Dharma check. If the P'o botches, the KJ must make a positive Dharma check. KJ may spend an hour in meditation beforehand to add their Meditation to their Hun before making the contested roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:09:57-08:00","id":999822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=999706#post999706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the P'o is not the Shadow. The P'o is literally a demonic symbiote forged by the agony experienced by the animal part of the soul while the divine part of the soul was being punished. The Shadow is just the dark impulses of a Wraith given voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got that backward. The po goes to hell and is tortured, the hun stays around the body. Also, DKoJ had the wraiths calling their shadow a po.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:31:07-08:00","id":999835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992607-the-kindred-of-the-east-hengeiyokai-thread?p=999706#post999706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the P'o is not the Shadow. The P'o is literally a demonic symbiote forged by the agony experienced by the animal part of the soul while the divine part of the soul was being punished. The Shadow is just the dark impulses of a Wraith given voice.<br /> <br /> Black Wind and Celerity were fairly well balanced in Revised, so I think that it should seek to maintain that balance. I have suggested one version that may keep the relative balance between the two Disciplines. I think that it is interesting to discuss it further though, and I hope that anyone working on KotE 20th will eventually look at our discussion.<br /> <br /> Now, I do think that it would be interesting to allow the Hun to be able to wrest additional Demon Chi from the P'o. Perhaps a PC could spend one point of Willpower to make a contested roll between the P'o and Hun (difficulty 6). If the Hun succeeds, each net success gives the KJ one point of Demon Chi. If the P'o succeeds, the KJ enters Shadow Soul for a scene. If neither succeeds, the KJ is paralyzed for one turn. If the Hun botches, the KJ must make a negative Dharma check. If the P'o botches, the KJ must make a positive Dharma check. KJ may spend an hour in meditation beforehand to add their Meditation to their Hun before making the contested roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The P'o absolutely is the Shadow, or at least the same part of the soul as the Shadow but manifesting slightly differently. It's even suggested you Shadowguide it. The main difference is that a KJ's Hun and P'o are reunified and thus don't work against each other in the same way the Psyche and Shadow do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}